WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.502
Tachyons can travel faster than light,

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.305
which means they should travel backward in time.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.640
Could they be used to make some kind of telephone

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.243
that would allow us to talk to our past selves?

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.412
No. No, they can't.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.915
[Intro Music]

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.017
Hey Crazies.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:21.154
Aside from the fact that tachyons are purely hypothetical particles,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.391
they could not be used this way, even if they did exist.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:27.627
The order of cause and effect must be maintained.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.363
Causality shall not be violated!

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.966
[Phone Ringing]

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:34.968
Hello?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.837
(Phone): Look, I know you’re excited, but don’t get ahead of yourself.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:38.972
(Phone): Start at the beginning.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.609
Oh yeah. I guess I should probably explain what a tachyon is first.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.945
Most particles travel slower than light.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:50.250
We call them bradyons because “brady-” is Greek for “slow.”

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:55.221
Some particles, like photons and gluons, travel at exactly the speed of light.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:59.359
We call them luxons because “lux” is Greek for “light.”

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:02.829
You're probably noticing a pattern here. Scientists love Greek.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:07.600
That means any particle traveling faster than light should be called a tachyon.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.203
“Tachy-” being Greek for “swift.”

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.339
Unsurprisingly, none of these particles can do that.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.508
None of them are tachyons.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:19.079
We've never detected a tachyon. We're not even sure if we could.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:23.483
But math doesn't say they can't exist, so what if they did?

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:27.120
Let's begin with what we know and then maybe we can extrapolate.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.157
Consider an electron inside a very long particle accelerator.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.860
The longer it travels, the faster it goes.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.197
The faster it goes, the slower its clock ticks.

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:41.434
To be clear, this isn't an actual clock. Electrons don't wear watches.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:47.440
In physics, a “clock” is just shorthand for the passage of local physical time.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.979
Basically, if we were to take a measurement of time in a reliable way, what would that tell us?

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:56.783
In this case, whatever processes this electron experiences,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.452
it experiences them slower than normal

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.821
As the electron approaches the speed of light,

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:05.191
time slows to an almost standstill for it.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.193
If this pattern were to continue,

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.663
time would completely stop at exactly the speed of light

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.366
and reverse when the speed of light is exceeded...

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.301
...like we'd see with the tachyon.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:19.539
So let's say this is a tachyon phone, also known as an anti-telephone,

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.842
and I want to call my past self at the beginning of this video.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.177
What would that take?

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.479
You're going to do a spacetime diagram, aren't you?

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.181
Yep, you called it.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:33.286
As a refresher, location is measured along the horizontal and time along the vertical.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.287
Why?

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.655
Tradition!

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:39.626
Since I haven't changed location, my path looks something like this.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:43.730
As time passes, I simply move up, which is forward in time.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:47.100
This is me now and this is me from a few minutes ago.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.102
If I were to use an ordinary phone,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:53.139
my signal would go forward in time along these diagonals.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:57.744
Radio is a type of light ...and all light travels along those diagonals.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:00.213
They form my future light cone.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:04.017
Inside it are all the slower than light particles I can send.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.753
Outside it are the faster than light paths.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.022
This is where tachyons travel.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.124
The bigger the angle is from my path,

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:14.194
the faster the particle is going relative to me.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:16.696
Though, to get a signal to my past self,

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.399
the tachyons would have to go straight down.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.400
Fast fast!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.804
That's an angle of 180 degrees though. How fast is that exactly?

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:28.074
We can convert to speed using this simple equation.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:32.111
The tangent of 180 degrees is... zero?

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.080
Hold on a second!

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.685
If we graph the tangent function across all angles, we get something like this.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:43.323
The speed of light is right here, which is 45 degrees along the diagonal...

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:45.058
exactly as expected.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.860
All slower than light particles are below that.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.829
Tachyons are above that.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:53.166
But look at this. It's broken at 90 degrees.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:58.605
As the tachyon speeds up, it approaches 90 degrees in the spacetime diagram.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:03.042
At 90 degrees, the tachyon would be traveling at infinite speed.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.445
What does anything above that even mean?

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:08.047
I guess we should be more careful with extrapolation.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.349
Yeah, exactly.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:12.919
Math is a tool and, like any tool, you have to know how to use it.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:18.858
Saying a clock goes in reverse is not the same as saying something travels back in time.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:23.763
In the spacetime diagram, these paths go back in time, but these go forward.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:27.166
So, clearly, not all tachyons go backward in time.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.302
Maybe some, but not all.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:32.305
The boundary between them is infinite speed.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:36.576
That would put those tachyons at every point in space at that moment.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:39.846
What Star Trek Voyager would call “Warp 10.”

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.180
(Emily off camera) Only Voyager?

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.584
It was mentioned in one episode of Voyager and then never brought up again.

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:47.053
(Emily off camera) Gotcha.
(Nick) We’re not going to talk about that episode anymore.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:51.491
That's an infinite discontinuity between the two types of tachyons.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:56.496
For the slowest tachyons that do go back in time, you’d get a negative speed.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.465
Not a negative velocity. A negative speed.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:04.304
And that's true all the way up to the 180 degrees we needed to go straight backward.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:07.140
That's not all that weird if it goes back in time, though, right?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.107
Okay. Okay.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:11.978
Let's keep going and assume that backward tachyons are possible.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:15.248
They're not, but let's assume they are for a couple more minutes.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:19.819
How do we get paths like this, if this path is infinite speed?

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:22.121
How do we get over that discontinuity?

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:25.024
Your first thought might be to send it from another location.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.727
Unfortunately, we'd run into the same problem.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:31.164
I might not need 180 degrees from here to get to the past,

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.933
but I'd still need an angle larger than 90.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:37.970
I would need to somehow make tachyons go faster than infinite speed,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.839
which I can't do.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.407
Or maybe I can.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.276
What if we give them a boost?

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:44.644
A Lorentz boost.

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:49.082
What if we bounce the tachyon signal off something that's already moving?

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:53.152
Like this probe zipping away at 80% the speed of light?

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.322
For this to work, the probe must have started its journey

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:59.525
before the time in the past I'm trying to reach.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.495
Creating an anti-telephone takes preparation.

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:06.432
Let's say my tachyon signal travels at five times the speed of light.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:11.437
That corresponds to an angle of almost 79 degrees in a spacetime diagram,

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:14.774
which is less than infinite speed and still toward the future.

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:18.611
That signal is received by the probe at just the right moment

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.980
and then retransmit it back toward me,

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.649
again at five times the speed of light.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.853
But here's the thing. That signal wasn't sent by me.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.554
It was sent by the probe.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:32.191
And that probe is traveling at 80% the speed of light

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.127
or about 38 degrees,

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:37.697
which means its coordinates are not the same as mine.

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:41.534
The probe might think it's sending a signal at 79 degrees.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:44.737
but this is what that looks like in our coordinates.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:50.943
The signal gets a boost of 38 degrees, putting the total angle at 117.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:53.846
That doesn’t look like 117 degrees!

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:57.150
Okay. Okay. I'll admit there's some distortion in this picture.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.819
It's important to understand that, in relativity,

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:02.889
it's the coordinates that change, not the paths.

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:06.125
But, if you insist, we can undistort the axes.

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:09.162
Now it actually looks like 117 degrees.

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:14.300
Since that angle is greater than 90, we've successfully sent a signal into the past.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.368
(Phone): Hello?

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:18.204
Look, I know you're excited, but don't get ahead of yourself.

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.572
Start at the beginning.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:20.973
What about causality, though?

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.775
Didn't you say it can't be broken?

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:23.876
Yes, I did.

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:27.880
Now, let me explain why Past Me will never receive that message.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:32.618
That rebound signal might be traveling at five times the speed of light for the probe,

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:37.256
but, in Past Me’s coordinates, it's much slower and away from him...

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.192
...like in the opposite direction.

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:44.197
According to Past Me, the signal never arrives, which means he isn't affected by it.

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:47.033
Causality shall not be violated!

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:49.869
So, wait, how did I receive that message earlier?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.804
Whatever.

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:53.906
Causality always wins.

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:56.576
But this isn't the only weird thing about tachyons.

00:07:56.576 --> 00:08:00.246
Just like ordinary particles can't accelerate to the speed of light,

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:02.915
tachyons can't decelerate to it.

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.717
They're trapped in FTL.

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:09.489
To make matters worse, the faster they go, the lower their total energy.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:14.861
If a tachyon goes fast enough, its total energy can be less than its rest energy.

00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:16.395
Absolutely absurd!

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:19.866
And, if we look a little deeper, we can see where the problem is.

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:22.602
This is the equation for relativistic momentum.

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:26.439
For slower than light particles, we get fairly ordinary values.

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:29.408
You plug in the mass and the speed and you get an answer.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:33.012
For speed of light particles, we get a zero in the denominator.

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:37.016
The only way that's allowed is if you also have a zero in the numerator.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:41.387
In other words, photons can't go that fast unless they have zero mass.

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:44.590
For tachyons, the denominator is imaginary,

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:47.760
which means the mass must also be imaginary.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:50.930
What I'm trying to say here is “tachyons are imaginary.”

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:55.234
Just because something is mathematically possible, that doesn't make it real.

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:58.304
Math always gives us an answer to our question,

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.973
even when our question isn't about reality.

00:09:00.973 --> 00:09:04.844
And until next time, remember, it's okay to be a little crazy.

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:08.281
I just want to take a moment to thank everyone who supports the channel.

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.616
Your generosity really makes a difference.

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:15.154
A special thanks goes out to our new asylum counselor, Richard Senegor;

00:09:15.154 --> 00:09:21.861
our new asylum orderlies, Chloe Joan Lopez, James Smith, Joel Wolhendler, and Peter Engrav;

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:26.933
and our new Einsteinium crazies, Sheila Owen and Matias Cveczilberg.

00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:29.468
Thank you so much for all of your support.

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:34.674
You should have used a hyperbola instead of a circle. Spacetime is hyperbolic.

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:38.177
Actually, you can use either one depending on your choice of axes.

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:39.912
The circle might be unconventional,

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:43.015
but it's mathematically valid if you move some terms around.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.483
Anyway, thanks for watching.

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:53.359
I want more feeling!

00:09:53.359 --> 00:09:55.528
How do you say “causality” with feeling?

